MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turns agent_tasks into work MiniMe can hand to a team member and follow up
on autonomously: assign → accept → remind before due → chase when overdue →
escalate to owner when the assignee goes silent → complete (+photo) → notify
the customer. Fills the gap where dm_team_member fired a one-off message with
zero tracking.

- migration 029: extend agent_tasks type+status CHECKs (delegated_task,
  blocked), add due_at / chase bookkeeping / assignee_message_id columns,
  suppliers workload columns, agent_task_events audit table, and indexes
  (incl. suppliers.contact_telegram, previously unindexed).
- delegation.js: pickAssignee (workload + specialty), trust-gated
  proposeAssignment (Supervised asks owner / Trusted auto-assigns), assignTask
  reusing jobFanout.generateBrief, the chase state machine, escalation,
  completion fan-out, and inbound team-member status handling.
- delegationLogic.mjs: pure decision + ranking + active-hours helpers, unit
  tested (16 cases).
- crons: /api/cron/delegation (hourly chase engine — no sub-hourly scheduler
  exists in prod) and /api/cron/team-standup (6pm EAT rollup, opt-in).
- replyEngine: dtask_ callback branch (accept/decline/done/progress/blocked/
  photo/assign/reassign/owner_takes/cancel, with tapper authorization) and an
  inbound hook before the supplier short-circuit; falls through unchanged for
  non-team-members.
- delegate_task + task_status tools in the owner brain, delegate_task in the
  customer brain, and prompt routing so delegation verbs no longer hit
  dm_team_member.
- /api/agent/team now returns per-member open-task count and on-time rate.

