From fcec2cfa7d9c3169d03464d4db7da3a848f040a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:03:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: closed loop (client to member and back) as a real
 conversation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Increment 3: the agent hears the client, briefs the right team member with
the client's files attached, holds an actual conversation with them, and
briefs the client back when it's done — and it talks like a person, not a
form with buttons.

The prior delegation loop was a state machine wearing a chat costume:
emoji-headed cards and a button for every transition. No one replies to a
task card with "almost done, 30 min" or a voice note. This rebuilds the
member-facing side as a real conversation while keeping the owner-facing
approval flows (which DO benefit from buttons) unchanged.

- teamBrain.js: a tool-calling agent (mirrors agentBrain.js's shape) that
  texts team members in the owner's actual voice (tone/greeting_style/
  code_switch_style/sample_replies) — short lines, first names, no emoji
  headers, code-switches Amharic/English like the owner does. Reads implicit
  signals (a bare photo of finished work = done, 👍 = accepted). Negotiates
  same-day rescheduling on its own; escalates to the owner when the client's
  deadline is actually at risk, on scope/price, on refusal, or after real
  silence. Two hard floors baked into the prompt: always answers truthfully
  if asked whether it's a bot, and never lets a deadline slip without
  telling the owner. team_threads gives it conversation memory — previously
  every team send was a one-off message with no history.
- delegation.js: member inbound now normalizes voice/photo/document to text
  via the same transcription.js extractors the customer path already uses
  (voice notes were previously invisible to the delegation loop entirely),
  then hands off to teamBrain instead of a button-driven classifier.
  assignTask/pingAssignee no longer send member-facing keyboards — teamBrain
  composes and sends the opening message and every chase, worded fresh each
  time. forwardTaskFiles sends the client's photos/documents/voice/video for
  this job to the assignee, scoped to the exact conversation that created
  the task (the old jobFanout forwarder scoped only by customer_id with no
  business_id or thread filter, so it could leak an unrelated older chat's
  files, and silently dropped video even though it's stored on inbound).
  notifyCustomer is the one path every client-facing send goes through:
  trust-gated (Supervised queues the owner's approval, Trusted+ sends and
  tells them), and persists an outbound messages row + touches the
  conversation so the thread stays coherent — the old completeTask sent a
  bare hardcoded line and logged it nowhere.
- sendAs.js / sendAsLogic.mjs: channel abstraction for "send as the owner's
  personal Telegram vs the bot." Telegram's Business API only reaches chats
  the connection already covers, discovered lazily from inbound traffic and
  previously thrown away every request (an in-memory Map). biz_conn_chats
  persists that coverage; sendAsOwnerOrBot tries personal only when proven
  reachable and ALWAYS falls back to the bot on failure — previously a
  rejected personal-identity send just vanished with no fallback. Also fixes
  a live bug: several call sites (cron/agent-tasks, agent/owner-tasks) handed
  a tenant's own bot token to code that attaches the shared bot's business
  connection id, a guaranteed Telegram rejection for any custom-bot tenant
  with Secretary Mode on.
- migration 031: source_conversation_id + client_briefed_at on agent_tasks
  (idempotency guard so a photo follow-up can't double-brief the client);
  contact_channel + ai_disclosed_at on suppliers; team_threads;
  biz_conn_chats.
- 20 new unit tests (chase eligibility, token selection, media-tag stripping,
  file-type mapping) — 77/77 full suite green; full next build passes.

